<%# The first screen of a new account.

    Sign-up lands here rather than on question one. A child who is dropped
    straight into a problem has no idea why they are being asked it, and the
    whole point of replacing the invisible calibration ladder was to say what
    is happening — so this says it, in three short lines, and the middle one is
    the one that matters: there is no failing this.

    Skippable on purpose. A child who wants to get on with it can, and the card
    on the home page waits for them. %>
<% content_for :bare, true %>

<div class="practice-shell math-fade" data-trace-mask>
  <div class="practice-column flex flex-1 flex-col gap-6 sm:justify-center">
    <div class="animate-rise flex flex-col gap-6">
      <span class="grid size-[72px] place-items-center rounded-[20px] bg-primary-50 text-primary-700">
        <%= render "shared/icon", name: :target, size: 36, stroke: 2 %>
      </span>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5">
        <h1 class="text-[32px] font-black leading-[1.15] tracking-[-.02em] text-ink-900">
          <%= t("placement.intro_title", name: current_user.name.split.first) %>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lead font-semibold leading-normal text-ink-700">
          <%= t("placement.intro_sub", count: Placement::QUESTION_COUNT) %>
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3.5">
        <% %w[length honest result].each do |point| %>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-base font-bold leading-normal text-ink-700">
            <span class="grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary-100 text-primary-800">
              <%= render "shared/icon", name: :check, size: 16, stroke: 3 %>
            </span>
            <span class="pt-1"><%= t("placement.intro_points.#{point}", count: Placement::QUESTION_COUNT) %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 max-sm:mt-auto">
      <%= button_to t("placement.intro_start"), placements_path, class: "button button-primary button-large" %>
      <%= link_to t("placement.later"), home_path, class: "button button-quiet button-large" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
